assertion  XSH.iswupper.001
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswupper() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class upper as the locale definition lists it: the 26
           uppercase letters.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswupper.002
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswupper() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the lowercase letters, the digits, the punctuation, the
           white-space characters and the controls.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswupper.003
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswupper(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswupper.004
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each uppercase letter c: iswlower(towlower(c)) is non-zero,
           towupper(towlower(c)) equals c, and iswupper(c) is non-zero while
           iswlower(c) is 0.
test       t/004-upper-lower-mapping.c

assertion  XSH.iswupper.005
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswupper.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswupper() is still non-zero for the 26
           uppercase letters.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
